From 8fa60dbf11fbff5121ae133c309cb4ba70834b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:39:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 182/307] fix: close the three wall-leak channels (roof light
 panel case)

User experiment (sun-blocking box over the roof killed the bright
ceiling; probe balls showed real energy in interior cells) pinned the
leak to three stacked holes, all closed:

- Isotropic bounce re-emission: the surface cache stored no normal, so a
  sunlit roof cell re-emitted half of its energy straight down into the
  interior. Accumulator widened 20 -> 24 ints/cell (average surface
  normal + pad); re-emission is now a cosine lobe along the average
  normal, with a weak isotropic fallback for incoherent-normal cells.
- Blanket first-iteration occlusion exemption: meant to let VPLs leave
  their own wall cells, it effectively granted every wall one free
  crossing - which is why r_LPVOcclusion 100 only hardened the leak
  edges. The first iteration now gates with the destination cell GV
  (the source cell never blocks its own exit, the receiving cell always
  applies); later iterations keep the midpoint average.
- VPL landing inside its own wall cell: with the surface in the sun-ward
  half of the cell the fixed 0.5-cell bias does not cross the boundary,
  so flux sat inside the roof cell where far-side receivers pick it up
  via the trilinear lookup. If the VPL cell equals the surfel cell it is
  now pushed one more cell along the dominant normal axis.

